From bc6c1600df5a8ef824917059c24e267561f7e5c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:06:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 066/108] gpu: dead-transfer skip also for full-screen color
 passes (battle transfers 3.5 -> 2.5 ms)

- gpu_skip_overwritten_transfers now also cuts the covered area out of
  ownership transfers when the draw writes color render targets completely
  (full write mask, no blending, depth test off or ALWAYS, no stencil
  rejection, no alpha test / alpha-to-mask / pixel kill, full MSAA mask), and
  every render target of the draw is overwritten (the cut-out is shared by the
  transfer call). gpu_skip_overwritten_color_transfers (default true) turns
  the color part off.
- DrawExtentEstimator::EstimateRectangleCoverage: a single triangle (e.g. a
  full-screen triangle) counts if it contains the scissor rectangle (limited
  to the viewport for clipped draws); 4-vertex triangle fans count as quads.
- Battle, same fight: transfers 3.5-3.6 -> 2.5 ms per frame, GPU work
  14.0 -> 13.2-13.3 Mcycles at ~492 MHz (was ~550); battle-start frames with
  and without it look the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

