   // shader on the CPU and returns the pixels the rectangle covers fully (right
   // and bottom exclusive, window offset and viewport clipping applied, scissor
   // not applied). reject_out (optional) tells why not, for diagnostics.
-  bool EstimateRectangleCoverage(const Shader& vertex_shader, int32_t& left_out,
-                                 int32_t& top_out, int32_t& right_out, int32_t& bottom_out,
-                                 uint32_t* reject_out = nullptr);
+  // A single triangle (a 1-triangle triangle list, e.g. a full-screen
+  // triangle) is accepted too if it contains the whole bounds rectangle
+  // (pixels, right / bottom exclusive, usually the scissor), which is then
